                <pb facs="0845" n="749" sameAs="frus:frus1879/pg749"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 2 in No. 849.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Foster to Mr. Newton.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[By telegraph.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1878-11-29"><hi rendition="#italic">November</hi> 29,
                        1878</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p rendition="#flush"><hi rendition="#small-caps">F. A. Newton</hi>, <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Guadalajara:</hi></p>
                <p>I regard tax as clearly unconstitutional, according to decision supreme court,
                    Goribar case. Bat being general and levied equally, I would not feel authorized
                    to intervene without express instructions from Washington. Americans subject to
                    same taxes as Mexicans. Is a question of law. Remedy may be had by resort to
                    courts for amparo.</p>
                <closer><signed>JOHN W. FOSTER.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
